Note: The numbers and symbols in the image are not standard musical notation, but rather a representation of notes or chords using different characters to indicate their position on an instrument's fretboard.
The first row represents 4th finger (index) note with dot above it. Second line is for second hand rest symbol which means no sound produced by that particular string at this point in time while playing the guitar, third one shows a half dash indicating partial bend or pull of strings to change pitch slightly and forthly indicates full duration without any pause between two notes.
The last row represents 0th finger (ring) note with dot above it.
